@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-operator`

-- g3-tests-operator.l4: tests of section 18, written by ENCODER G3.
--
-- Every expected value was decided from the Hebrew text of s.18 (inputs/law.wiki lines 152-155, checked against the gazette page 186)
-- and from the Third Schedule items (5) and (6) (law.wiki lines 718-721) before the module was run.
-- The licence kinds that cover a system follow section 2: grade 1 up to 18 kW, grade 2 up to 70 kW, grade 3 any system; so a system of
-- 10 kW is covered by all three kinds, one of 25 kW by grades 2 and 3, one of 80 kW by grade 3 only.  (The covering lists are inputs
-- from the licensing group; they are written out here as illustrations of its answer.)
-- `-- TRACE-EXPECT:` lines are read by check-traces.py.

§ `Tests of section 18`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN regular IS A BOOLEAN
      business IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
`fixture — a person who` regular `and` business MEANS
    `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` WITH
        `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems` IS regular
        `owns or manages a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public` IS business

GIVETH A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
`fixture — a regular engager with no business` MEANS `fixture — a person who` TRUE `and` FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
`fixture — an owner of a public business who does not regularly engage` MEANS `fixture — a person who` FALSE `and` TRUE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
`fixture — a regular engager who owns a public business` MEANS `fixture — a person who` TRUE `and` TRUE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
`fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner` MEANS `fixture — a person who` FALSE `and` FALSE

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 10 kilowatts` MEANS LIST `grade 1 licence`, `grade 2 licence`, `grade 3 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` MEANS LIST `grade 2 licence`, `grade 3 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 80 kilowatts` MEANS LIST `grade 3 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — grade 1 only` MEANS LIST `grade 1 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — grade 2 only` MEANS LIST `grade 2 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — grade 3 only` MEANS LIST `grade 3 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — grades 1 and 2` MEANS LIST `grade 1 licence`, `grade 2 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — no kind` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A Person
`fixture — Cool Ltd, a corporation that is the operator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "C-500", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

§§ `18(a). The operator may engage only a person with the appropriate licence`

-- "A licence of the kind appropriate to perform work on that system": one of the kinds in force is among the kinds that cover the system.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grade 2 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grade 3 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 10 kilowatts`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grade 3 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 80 kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grade 2 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 80 kilowatts`
-- A person with two kinds in force needs only one of them to fit.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grades 1 and 2` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grades 1 and 2` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 80 kilowatts`
-- No licence in force fits no system; a system no kind is said to cover is covered by nobody's licence.
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 10 kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator may engage the person` `fixture — grade 3 only` `fixture — no kind`

-- The breach: an operator, once the Law has commenced for the work, in an engagement in work on a cooling system, of a person without the appropriate licence.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
-- Not an operator: nothing is breached.
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
-- The Law has not commenced for the work; the act is not work on a cooling system.
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` FALSE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE FALSE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`

-- The Third Schedule splits the breach: item (5) no licence at all, item (6) a licence not of the appropriate kind.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 80 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` FALSE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Alternative S18-H: a licence the person still holds but that is not in force counts as a licence held, so item (6) and not item (5).
-- Taken: a person whose only licence has lapsed has none "in his hand" in force, so item (5).
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a), a licence held but not in force being a licence held` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`
-- Holding nothing at all is item (5) under both readings.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a), a licence held but not in force being a licence held` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
-- A licence in force but not appropriate is item (6) under both.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a), a licence held but not in force being a licence held` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`

-- Alternative S18-D: if the definition of "operator" in s.18(c), "in this section", did not reach the Third Schedule, items (5) and (6) could not be applied.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a), the word operator of the Third Schedule being undefined` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` BECAUSE "s.18(c): the word operator is defined only for section 18, so Third Schedule items (5) and (6), which use it, cannot be applied to anyone"

-- The record Chapter 6 takes: the violator is the operator, here a corporation; the day of the act is the day of the engagement.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — Cool Ltd, a corporation that is the operator` "act-18-1" (YMD 2026 5 4) `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST (Violation WITH `the violator` IS `fixture — Cool Ltd, a corporation that is the operator`, `the listed violation` IS `engaging a person who had no licence at all`, `reference for the act` IS "act-18-1", `date of the act` IS YMD 2026 5 4)
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the violation committed under section 18(a)` `fixture — Cool Ltd, a corporation that is the operator` "act-18-2" (YMD 2026 5 4) `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The prohibition as a rule: standing, breached by the engagement of an unlicensed person, untouched by the engagement of a licensed one.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.18(a): the operator engaged a person in work on a cooling system who held no licence of the kind appropriate to the system
#TRACE `s.18(a) — the operator shall not engage a person in work on a cooling system without a licence of the appropriate kind` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 1 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the operator` DOES `engage a person in work on a cooling system` AT 4
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | engage a person in work on a cooling system
#TRACE `s.18(a) — the operator shall not engage a person in work on a cooling system without a licence of the appropriate kind` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the operator` DOES `engage a person in work on a cooling system` AT 4
-- No sunset: the prohibition stands a year later.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | engage a person in work on a cooling system
#TRACE `s.18(a) — the operator shall not engage a person in work on a cooling system without a licence of the appropriate kind` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Not an operator: the rule owes nothing.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.18(a) — the operator shall not engage a person in work on a cooling system without a licence of the appropriate kind` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the operator` DOES `engage a person in work on a cooling system` AT 4

§§ `18(b). The operator must make sure that the licensees work to the Standard`

GIVEN sufficient IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)`
`fixture — measures` sufficient MEANS
    `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)` WITH
        `the measures were sufficient to make sure that the licensee would work to the Standard` IS sufficient

-- The duty concerns a licensee the operator engages: an operator, once the Law has commenced for the work, in work on a cooling system, with a licensee.
#ASSERT `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` FALSE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — section 18(b) applies to the engagement of a licensee` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE FALSE `fixture — grade 2 only`
-- Taken (fork S18-B): a duty of conduct.  Sufficient measures are the steps; insufficient ones are the breach.
#ASSERT `s.18(b) — the operator took the section 18(b) steps` (`fixture — measures` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator took the section 18(b) steps` (`fixture — measures` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` (`fixture — measures` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` FALSE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` FALSE)
-- Alternative S18-B: a duty of result.  The two readings part on a licensee whose work failed the Standard despite sufficient measures ...
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b), the duty being one of result` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` FALSE
-- ... and on insufficient measures whose licensee nevertheless worked to the Standard.
#ASSERT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b), the duty being one of result` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` TRUE
-- The alternative too is limited to an engaged licensee of an operator.
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b), the duty being one of result` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b), the duty being one of result` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` FALSE

-- The duty as a rule: a MUST with no deadline.  Discharged by steps that suffice; standing otherwise (no deadline, so no breach can be traced).
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.18(b) — the operator must make sure that the licensee works to the Standard` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the operator` DOES `take steps to make sure that the licensees engaged work to the Standard` AT 10
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | take steps to make sure that the licensees engaged work to the Standard
#TRACE `s.18(b) — the operator must make sure that the licensee works to the Standard` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the operator` DOES `take steps to make sure that the licensees engaged work to the Standard` AT 10
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | take steps to make sure that the licensees engaged work to the Standard
#TRACE `s.18(b) — the operator must make sure that the licensee works to the Standard` `fixture — a regular engager with no business` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.18(b) — the operator must make sure that the licensee works to the Standard` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner` TRUE TRUE `fixture — grade 2 only` (`fixture — measures` FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `18(c). Who is an operator`

-- "One who regularly engages another ... whether or not he holds a licence, and including an owner or manager of a business offering such work
-- to the public."  Taken (fork S18-C): each limb is enough.
#ASSERT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator` `fixture — a regular engager with no business`
#ASSERT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator` `fixture — an owner of a public business who does not regularly engage`
#ASSERT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator` `fixture — a regular engager who owns a public business`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner`
-- Alternative S18-C: the business limb only illustrates the first; the owner who does not regularly engage is not an operator.
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator, the business limb being only an illustration` `fixture — an owner of a public business who does not regularly engage`
#ASSERT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator, the business limb being only an illustration` `fixture — a regular engager with no business`
#ASSERT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator, the business limb being only an illustration` `fixture — a regular engager who owns a public business`
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator, the business limb being only an illustration` `fixture — neither a regular engager nor an owner`
-- The discriminating case is an owner of a business offering such work to the public who engages an unlicensed person once and not regularly:
-- an operator (so the engagement is item (5)) on the taken reading, not on the alternative.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` `fixture — an owner of a public business who does not regularly engage` TRUE TRUE `fixture — no kind` `fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
